.TH CHTTP_BASE64_ENCODE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_encode \- encode a buffer as base64 (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

char *chttp_base64_encode(const void *data, size_t len,
                          size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a static inline wrapper around chttp_base64_encode_mp() that
gives NULL for the memory management procedures, so the function uses
malloc and free.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
data     The buffer to encode. It can be NULL only if len is 0.
len      The number of bytes in data.
out_len  Optional; it gets the length of the string that the
         function gives back, not counting the terminating NUL.
         Give NULL to ignore it.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new NUL-terminated base64 string on success.
NULL if the allocation fails, if data is NULL and len is not zero, or
if len is so large that the encoded size overflows size_t.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_encode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_decode (3)
